    - target: {fileID: 4711005256018735203, guid: 0daf8292e6fd6cf46a68c89d3a946ace, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "The 4 month internship at nighingames (September - December 2025) granted
        me the opportunity to work at an indie game studio. I worked on \"Loxia\"
        using Unreal Engine and a prototype for a desktop game in Unity. During this
        Internship i worked on Code, Blueprints, Post processing and Material Functions.\n\nAbout
        Loxia:\nLoxia is made Entirely in Unreal Engine 5. It is a Game where you
        play as a nun in the 13th century, collecting herbs to heal various patients.
        Loxia was the current in house projekt of nightingames. As a technical artist
        i was allowed to work on various material functions and postprocessing effects,
        code for the patients,  and various UI Modifications. \n\nAbout the Unity
        Prototype:\nI worked on this prototype mostly on my own for a month. To do
        this, i set up my own repository, project etc. Notably, i worked on the Game
        Logik and used Win32 to read user data from windows.\n\nTools:\nOrganisation:
        Jira, Confluence, Discord\nDevelopment: UE5, Unity, Visual Studio 2022, Git
        & Fork\n\nLearnings:\nImportance of good dokumentation\nProgramming with
        a game design department in mind\nUse of UE\nUse of Win32 API\nDefinition
        of Goals and Tasks\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
